  "lines" : [
    {
      "fontSize" : 8,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        425.95999999999998,
        748.51210000000003,
        125.04000000000002,
        9.3120000000000118
      ],
      "text" : "Conducting Monetary Policy 21"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        692.64010000000007,
        410.09299999999973,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "What is monetary policy? It is the Federal Reserve’s actions, as a central bank, to achieve the"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        676.64010000000007,
        405.04599999999988,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "“dual mandate” goals specified by Congress: maximum employment and stable prices in the"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        660.64010000000007,
        62.800000000000011,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "United States."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        628.64010000000007,
        427.59599999999978,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "The Federal Reserve conducts monetary policy by using a variety of tools to manage financial con-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        612.64010000000007,
        428.09399999999982,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "ditions that encourage progress toward its dual mandate objectives. Monetary policy most directly"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        596.64010000000007,
        419.99499999999978,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "affects the current and expected future path of short-term interest rates; the anticipated path of"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        580.64010000000007,
        411.64299999999969,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "short-term interest rates then affects overall financial conditions including longer-term interest"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        564.64010000000007,
        423.64499999999987,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "rates, stock prices, the exchange value of the dollar, and many other asset prices. Through these"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        548.64010000000007,
        425.49399999999991,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "channels, monetary policy influences the decisions of households and businesses, thus affecting"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        532.64010000000007,
        429.44000000000005,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "overall spending, investment, production, employment, and inflation in the United States (figure 3.1)."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        324.64010000000007,
        425.39499999999987,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "Conducting monetary policy effectively involves a number of important elements including a basic"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        308.64010000000007,
        415.34299999999996,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "strategy that guides the adjustment of the stance of policy over time, a policy process involving"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        292.64010000000007,
        427.34299999999962,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "the coordinated actions of the Federal Reserve’s two decisionmaking bodies—the Board of Gover-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        276.64010000000007,
        423.84299999999985,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "nors (Board) and the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC)—a communications effort with the"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        260.64010000000007,
        418.79399999999976,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "public to describe the rationale for the Federal Reserve’s policy decisions, a range of tools used"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        244.64010000000007,
        417.94399999999968,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "to implement the desired stance of policy, and an institutional framework that involves appropri-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        228.64010000000007,
        427.69699999999966,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "ate independence of the Federal Reserve in conducting policy while remaining fully accountable to"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        212.64010000000007,
        219.19999999999999,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "Congress and the American people for its actions."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 16,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        161.1361,
        377.83679999999993,
        18.944000000000017
      ],
      "text" : "The Federal Reserve’s Monetary Policy Mandate and"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 16,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        143.1361,
        204.95680000000004,
        18.944000000000017
      ],
      "text" : "Strategy and Why It Matters"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        121.43610000000001,
        413.44299999999981,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "The Federal Reserve was created by Congress in 1913 to provide the nation with a safer, more"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        105.43610000000001,
        427.69299999999987,
        11.640000000000001
      ],
      "text" : "flexible, and more stable monetary and financial system. In 1977, Congress amended the Federal"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        89.43610000000001,
        424.59399999999971,
        11.640000000000001
      ],
      "text" : "Reserve Act (FRA) to provide greater clarity about the goals of monetary policy. The amended FRA"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        73.43610000000001,
        402.0449999999999,
        11.640000000000001
      ],
      "text" : "directs the Board of Governors and the FOMC to conduct monetary policy “so as to promote"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        102.5,
        494.14010000000002,
        367.59599999999989,
        11.839999999999975
      ],
      "text" : "Figure 3.1. The Fed’s statutory mandate: maximum employment and stable prices"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 8,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        102.5,
        477.15220000000005,
        394.99439999999976,
        9.3120000000000118
      ],
      "text" : "The Federal Reserve conducts monetary policy in pursuit of the goals set for it by Congress. The mandated goals"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 8,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        102.5,
        467.15220000000005,
        306.1968,
        9.3120000000000118
      ],
      "text" : "are considered essential to a well-functioning economy for households and businesses."
    }
